{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-22T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Tucked into the rugged coastline of northern Spain, the 16th-century Hermitage of Santa Justa, featured in today's image, overlooks the crashing waves of the Cantabrian Sea. Built partly into the rock and associated with the relics of Saints Justa and Rufina, the small chapel eventually became a pilgrimage site. Its sheltered stone walls create a striking contrast with the powerful waves and rugged cliffs around it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JustaHermitage_EN-GB3758221368_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JustaHermitage_EN-GB3758221368_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Shelter among the waves","Title":"The chapel and hermitage of Santa Justa in Cantabria, Spain","Copyright":"© Tramont_ana/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.42595,4.09762/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.42595,4.09762;S9;Santa Justa, Cantabria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261122_JustaHermitage\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ermita+Santa+Justa+chapel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261122_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261122_JustaHermitage"},"Ssd":"20261122","Name":"JustaHermitage","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3758221368","FullDateString":"22 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bathed in a sun-kissed glow, Nice is a patchwork of terracotta rooftops, historic churches and pastel façades along the French Riviera, as seen in today's image. Founded by the ancient Greeks and long associated with the Italian House of Savoy, Nice officially became part of France in 1860. Today, its layered past remains visible throughout this coastal city in the south of France, where historic architecture meets the blue waters of the Mediterranean and the sunlit hills of the Côte d'Azur.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RedNice_EN-GB3371662260_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RedNice_EN-GB3371662260_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Terracotta dreams","Title":"Nice, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France","Copyright":"© Siripong Kaewla-iad/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.70094,7.26839/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.70094,7.26839;S9;Nice, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261121_RedNice\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Nice+France&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261121_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261121_RedNice"},"Ssd":"20261121","Name":"RedNice","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3371662260","FullDateString":"21 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Kvaløya in Troms, northern Norway, humpback whales move through the cold Arctic waters in search of a proper feast. They visit the region in winter, following migrating herring into the fjords. Humpbacks are known for their remarkable feeding techniques, including bubble-net feeding, in which some whales blow rings or walls of bubbles to corral fish before surging upwards with their mouths open to catch their prey. In today's image, a humpback slips beneath the icy waves under a glowing pastel sky, capturing a moment of tranquillity in Norway's wild north.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_EN-GB2786065203_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_EN-GB2786065203_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Feasting in the fjords","Title":"Diving humpback whale, Kvaloya, Troms, Northern Norway","Copyright":"© Espen Bergersen/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/69.62389,18.53103/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=69.62389,18.53103;S9;Kvaloya, Troms, Norway&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=humpback+whales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261120_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera"},"Ssd":"20261120","Name":"Megaptera","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2786065203","FullDateString":"20 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"It's World Philosophy Day, when thinkers come together to explore life's enduring questions. To mark the occasion, today's image features \"Body of Knowledge\", a sculpture at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany. Created by Spanish artist Jaume Plensa, it combines steel letters from eight different alphabets to form a human figure. Plensa explains: 'Our body is the home of the spirit. The place in which ideas live.'","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-GB1364284090_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-GB1364284090_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Where ideas take shape","Title":"The \"Body of Knowledge\" sculpture by Jaume Plensa at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany","Copyright":"© Todamo/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.127805,8.667807/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.127805,8.667807;S9;Goethe University, Frankfurt&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Philosophy+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261119_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture"},"Ssd":"20261119","Name":"KnowledgeSculpture","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1364284090","FullDateString":"19 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These barn owls, bathed in the evening light, are waiting for the hunt to begin. As night falls, the birds of prey swoop into action, listening for the faint movements of mice and voles in the grass and leaves. Their heart-shaped faces help funnel sound towards their exceptionally sensitive ears, allowing them to locate prey with remarkable precision in the dark. They then swoop down almost silently, their soft feathers helping to muffle the sound of their approach.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-GB9873814926_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-GB9873814926_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hunting from dusk till dawn","Title":"Pair of barn owls","Copyright":"© Zahoor Salmi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Barn owls don't hoot; they make eerie, screeching noises, which might explain their reputation as harbingers of doom.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+owl&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261118_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite"},"Ssd":"20261118","Name":"BarnOwlsUnite","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"9873814926","FullDateString":"18 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today's image features the Trail of the Cedars, one of 1,126 kilometres of hiking trails in Glacier National Park, Montana. Its 1.4km-long loop includes a raised boardwalk which cuts a path through western red cedars and hemlock trees. The park boasts routes for all abilities, taking in alpine lakes, wildflower meadows, mountain passes and wilderness stretching to the Canadian border.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-GB2504891943_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-GB2504891943_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Step into the great outdoors","Title":"Trail of the Cedars, Glacier National Park, Montana, USA","Copyright":"© DBushue Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.706957,-113.817235/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.706957,-113.817235;S9;Glacier National Park, Montana&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Trail+of+the+Cedars+Glacier+National+Park+Montana&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261117_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars"},"Ssd":"20261117","Name":"TrailCedars","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2504891943","FullDateString":"17 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Incredible views and rock-solid foundations are part of the charm of these ancient dwellings, set into the cliffside in New Mexico. Nomads had long used the natural caves above Cliff Dweller Creek as temporary shelter, but it was the Native American Mogollon people who made them their home. Archaeologists believe they created dozens of rooms inside five alcoves in the 1270s and 1280s. Up to 15 families lived here at any one time, raising children, making pottery and overlooking the fertile Gila River valley where they grew crops and hunted wildlife. For reasons unknown, the Mogollon people moved on around 1300, leaving behind one of the American Southwest's most important archaeological sites.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-GB1863069273_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-GB1863069273_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Built to last","Title":"Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Chiara Salvadori/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/33.254028,108.272634/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=33.254028,108.272634;S9;Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Gila+Cliff+Dwellings+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261116_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff"},"Ssd":"20261116","Name":"GilaCliff","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1863069273","FullDateString":"16 Nov 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lit by streetlights as it crosses this narrow stretch of the Norwegian Sea, Sommarøy Bridge is the only road onto the small fishing island that shares its name. From a distance, with its white sand beaches and turquoise waters, you might think you were somewhere tropical. But Sommarøy lies north of the Arctic Circle, and those are icy waters you're crossing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_EN-GB9867775795_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_EN-GB9867775795_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Skimming the sea","Title":"Sommarøy Bridge from above, Tromso, Norway","Copyright":"© Roberto Moiola/Sysaworld/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/69.623346,18.045599/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=69.623346,18.045599;S9;Sommarøy Bridge, Norway&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sommar%c3%b8y+Norway&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261129_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge"},"Ssd":"20261129","Name":"SommaroyBridge","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"9867775795","FullDateString":"29 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"This autumn view from Letná Park looks out over Prague, which was built along the banks of the Vltava River in Czechia. In today's image, the river winds its way through the historic Old Town and Malá Strana districts, beneath Mánes Bridge in the foreground. Many beautiful bridges now span the Vltava, but for centuries there was only one: Charles Bridge, pictured second from the bottom. Its first stones were laid in 1357 during the reign of Charles IV and, until 1841, it was the only way to cross the river on foot. Today, its stone arches, Gothic towers and statues lining the bridge draw large crowds, so visitors are advised to arrive by dawn for the best photographs. Alternatively, they could walk on to the next crossing, Legion Bridge, which is less crowded and offers beautiful views of the National Theatre, Prague Castle and its busier neighbour.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_EN-GB9335121200_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_EN-GB9335121200_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Bridges through time","Title":"Old town and Vltava River, Prague, Czechia","Copyright":"© Lara_Uhryn/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.089959,14.412867/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.089959,14.412867;S9;Mánes Bridge, Prague&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Prague+bridges&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261128_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague"},"Ssd":"20261128","Name":"VltavaPrague","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"9335121200","FullDateString":"28 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Hidden within an ancient sandstone landscape, Face Canyon is one of 96 canyons stretching out from Lake Powell in southern Utah. Many are far from roads and would be difficult to reach if they hadn't been flooded by the lake, which was created in 1963 during the construction of the Glen Canyon Dam. The lake's waters extend for around 186 miles (299 kilometres), along creeks and canyons which you can explore by boat, kayak or jet ski.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_EN-GB5580459617_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_EN-GB5580459617_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Ribbons of grey and gold","Title":"Butte at sunset, Face Canyon, Lake Powell, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Jeff Foott/Minden","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.002262,-111.24176/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.002262,-111.24176;S9;Face Canyon, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Powell&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261127_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon"},"Ssd":"20261127","Name":"FaceCanyon","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5580459617","FullDateString":"27 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water, sunlight and lush greenery come together at Rainbow Falls in Hilo, on the island of Hawaii. Here, the Wailuku River plunges around 24 metres over a lava ledge, sending mist into the air as it reaches the pool below. On sunny mornings, the mist can catch the light and produce the colourful rainbows that gave the falls their name. Known in Hawaiian as Waiānuenue, meaning 'rainbow water', this striking waterfall is surrounded by tropical vegetation and has a special place in Hawaiian legend.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_EN-GB7287228600_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_EN-GB7287228600_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where rainbows fall","Title":"Rainbow Falls on the Wailuku River, Hilo, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© Peter Unger/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/19.718779,-155.108611/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=19.718779,-155.108611;S9;Rainbow Falls, Wailuku River&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rainbow+Falls+Wailuku+River+Hawaii&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261126_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo"},"Ssd":"20261126","Name":"RFHilo","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7287228600","FullDateString":"26 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Snow transforms Bryce Canyon National Park, blanketing the landscape in white while its fiery orange-red hoodoos rise above the snowy terrain. Seen from Sunset Point, one of the park's best-known viewpoints, these fantastical shapes are part of the Claron Formation, a collection of sedimentary rocks deposited around 50 million years ago and later sculpted by weathering and erosion. Because much of the park lies above 2,440 metres, snow can arrive as early as October. In today's image, snow clings to the canyon's ridges and spires while mist drifts across the cliffs, creating an iconic winter scene in the American Southwest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_EN-GB6418180336_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_EN-GB6418180336_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"When snow meets red rock","Title":"Sunset Point, Bryce Canyon National Park, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Colin D. Young/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.623535,-112.167279/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.623535,-112.167279;S9;Sunset Point, Bryce Canyon National Park, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bryce+Canyon+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261125_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint"},"Ssd":"20261125","Name":"SunsetPoint","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6418180336","FullDateString":"25 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As Britain's only native squirrel species, red squirrels thrive in Scotland's Cairngorms National Park. An important refuge, the park offers ancient Caledonian pine forests and more recently planted conifer woodlands, providing valuable habitat and food for squirrels foraging for Scots pine seeds, nuts and other tasty morsels throughout the year. In today's image, a red squirrel is perched amid warm orange and yellow leaves, looking right at home as it ponders its next move in the Scottish Highlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_EN-GB7505295031_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_EN-GB7505295031_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Autumnal camouflage","Title":"Red squirrel in Cairngorms National Park, Highlands, Scotland","Copyright":"© Scotland: The Big Picture/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/57.0833,-3.6667/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=57.0833,-3.6667;S9;Cairngorms National Park, Highlands, Scotland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eurasian+red+squirrel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261124_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel"},"Ssd":"20261124","Name":"CairngormsSquirrel","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7505295031","FullDateString":"24 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today's image shows the gradual coiling of a young fiddlehead's tip, echoing the geometric patterns seen throughout nature. In maths, the Fibonacci sequence follows a similar progression, each number formed by adding the two before it: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 and so on. Today is Fibonacci Day, chosen for the numbers of the date (11/23) to honour the sequence. Eventually the young fern frond shown here will unfurl as it grows, but elsewhere in the plant world, the sequence will continue to appear in the spiralling arrangements of sunflower heads, pinecones, succulents and pineapples.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_EN-GB6785963710_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_EN-GB6785963710_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Geometry in nature","Title":"Fiddlehead fern","Copyright":"© Reza Saputra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Fibonacci sequence was popularised through a 13th-century maths problem about multiplying rabbits.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=fibonacci+day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261123_0000\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern"},"Ssd":"20261123","Name":"FibonacciFern","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6785963710","FullDateString":"23 Nov 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Image of the day","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Learn more","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Quick fact:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Recent Homepage images",